# Impeccable Typeset Rules

Typesetting is about making text readable, scannable, and comfortable.

---

## Core Principle

Text should be easy to read and easy to scan.

If text feels dense or tiring → it must be improved.

---

## Readability

- Use comfortable font sizes
- Use sufficient line height:
  - `leading-relaxed`
  - `leading-7`
- Avoid cramped text

---

## Line Length

- Limit text width:
  - `max-w-2xl`
  - `max-w-3xl`
- Avoid full-width long paragraphs

---

## Hierarchy

- Titles must stand out
- Body text must be easy to read
- Secondary text must be lighter

Example:

- Title: `text-slate-900 font-semibold`
- Body: `text-slate-600`
- Meta: `text-slate-500`

---

## Paragraph Structure

- Break text into smaller chunks
- Use spacing between paragraphs:
  - `space-y-4`
- Avoid large text blocks

---

## Alignment

- Prefer `text-left` for readability
- Avoid centering long text

---

## Scanability

- Use:
  - short paragraphs
  - bullet points
  - clear sections
- Make content easy to skim

---

## Constraints

- Do not change logic
- Keep UI simple
- Maintain consistency across pages

---

## Goal

The UI should feel:

- readable
- clean
- comfortable
- easy to scan
